ery  stuttering as it tries to raise them one  last time the last time we saw  tormund Giantsbane and beric Dondarrion  at the end of season seven they were  caught up in the night Kings first  strike watching as he brought down the  wall when we finally get to check in  with them in season eight they're  tracking the destruction that the White  Walkers have left in their wake as they  traveled beyond the wall and they find a  pretty disturbing message left by the  night king the young Ned umber turned  into a white and pinned to a wall amidst  severed limbs provides the season's best  jump-scare when he really conds and has  to be set aflame it's one of the most  distressing images in the series recent  memory with umbers dead body at the  center of a spiral pattern made up of  body parts but it's not the first time  audiences have seen this pattern since  the very first episode of the show the  White Walkers have long been associated  with spirals and circles from arranging  the body parts of their victims to the  sacred place in the north and the cave  drawings that John showed Daenerys in  the seventh season perhaps most  crucially the spirals can be seen in the  scene that showed the children of the  forest creating the first walker  suggesting that these shapes have more  to do with the lore of the walkers than  viewers fully understand when audiences  first met Theon Greyjoy he was arrogant  and dismissive especially to Jon Snow  letting audiences know that perhaps  Theon needed to be taken down a peg put  away your blade take orders from your  father not you  eight seasons later and Theon's been  brought about as low as any character  possibly could he's been psychologically  broken from emotional and physical  torture leaving him a beaten man  struggling to reclaim himself and fight  for a cause he believes in after several  years of terrible behavior Theon has  fully redeemed himself by saving sonses  life and proving that he's willing to  sacrifice himself to do the right thing  now in the show's final season Theon  returned to Winterfell to fight for the  Starks even though his sister Yara  set off to retake the Iron Islands in  doing this the aunts journey has come  full circle  after starting out with the Starks  before abandoning them he has finally  come home to stand with them one last  time completing the arc of one of the  show's most troubled characters you're a  good man before she used it to put a  permanent end to the army of the Dead  arias Valyrian steel dagger already had  a pretty notable history it was first  seen in the show's second episode when  it was used in an attempt to murder bran  Stark after his fall from the tower but  it really belonged to Littlefinger  himself Lord Petyr Baelish from there it  stayed with Littlefinger until he gave  it back to bran who gave it to Arya who  naturally used it to execute  Littlefinger during his season seven  trial during the episodes big climax as  the night king makes his way towards  bran arias training helps her silently  move through the godswood until she gets  to the night king himself destroying him  with Littlefinger's dagger to save the  brother who gave it to her this knife  has had quite the journey where bran is  concerned  so it seems oddly fitting that the  weapon once intended to kill him is what  saved not just him but every human  fighting at Winterfell  Cersei spent the Battle of Winterfell  waiting out her enemies so when they  finally arrived at King's Landing to try  to force her surrender she was ready to  strike  maybe ceci will win and kill us all that  would solve all problems before the  fight began though she had one last  brutal insult to hand down to Daenerys  and her forces after her assault on  Daenerys ships near Dragonstone Cersei  captures Masson day Daenerys is  Translator confidant and best friend and  it's immediately clear that Cersei will  use her hostage however she has to in  order to achieve her bottom line  if you have any last words now is the  time in a brutal display of power  Cersei orders the beheading of poor  Musante who gives her life willingly for  her chosen Queen bravely standing in  support of the woman who freed her from  her chains  however Circe's decision to decapitate  Masson de wound up having much larger  consequences than she realized it was  one of the final things that drove  Daenerys over the edge leading directly  to the destruction of King's Landing and  to Cersei having a couple tons of bricks  dropped on her head she shouldn't have  been surprised though the last time a  blond Lannister ruler vindictively cut  off someone's head to prove a point  it was Joffrey ordering Ned Stark's  execution the act that kicked off seven  long years of warfare and prestige  television in the final days before her  death  Cersei became as sadistic as her  terrible son as one of the only  substances that can destroy a white  Walker Valyrian steel can be tough to  come by as a result only a small handful  of characters on Thrones are in  possession of weapons made out of it one  of those characters was Ned Stark  longtime warden of the north and Lord of  Winterfell and unfortunately short-lived  hand of the king to Robert Baratheon  whose family sword was a massive piece  of Valyrian steel called ice after the  honorable but naive Ned figured out that  Prince Joffrey wasn't Robert's  biological son he ended up losing his  head and ice was melted down and remade  into two new blades the first christened  widow's wail by Joffrey was barely used  before Joffrey met his own untimely end  it ended up with Jaime his uncle slash  father you said my father was my father  but my uncle is my father my father  the second sword Oathkeeper was gifted  to Brienne of Tarth though Jaime and  Brienne spent some time on opposing  sides of the conflict between the  Lannisters and the north they joined  forces again during the Battle of  Winterfell as they fought side-by-side  the two 